WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.030 --> 00:00:07.040
Climate change is the most urgent threat facing
human civilization today.

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:12.309
For the people of Bangladesh, rising seas,
flooding, salinity intrusion, cyclones, and

00:00:12.309 --> 00:00:18.680
extreme heat waves have already caused families
to lose their livelihoods, homes and communities.

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:21.690
Globally, Bangladesh is just the start.

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:25.520
These changes are accelerating. Within the next few decades,

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:28.970
climate change will force many millions to
migrate.

00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:35.769
MIT and BRAC will transform climate adaptation by creating CREWSNET, the Climate Resilience

00:00:35.769 --> 00:00:38.109
Early Warning System Network.

00:00:38.109 --> 00:00:43.629
CREWSNET puts cutting edge climate forecasting technology directly into the hands of individuals

00:00:43.629 --> 00:00:49.250
to show how future climate and extreme weather
patterns will impact their lives.

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:55.979
This technology, combined with access to innovative
power, water, agriculture, and financing services...will

00:00:55.979 --> 00:01:01.519
empower families, communities, and governments
to make and implement informed, proactive

00:01:01.519 --> 00:01:05.750
decisions about how to adapt to this changing
world.

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:10.710
This widely accessible, integrated tool will
enable civil society organizations to better

00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:15.940
support these choices, and strengthen efforts
to create climate resilient communities throughout

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:17.250
Bangladesh.

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:21.850
CREWSNET will serve as a model for people
everywhere facing similar threats to their

00:01:21.850 --> 00:01:24.049
livelihood and survival.

00:01:24.049 --> 00:01:28.859
Together, we can create a better future...
for Bangladesh and the world.

